<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 70.9 percent of their intended 3.8 million hectares of 1996/97 maize by November 15, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Sunflower sowing reached 68 percent of the 3.0 million hectares intended, a total which will be 11.9 percent down on last season. The area sown with soybeans reached 24.6 percent of the 6.3 million expected, an area 5.4 percent up on last year. Wheat harvesting reached 2.8 percent of the 6.8 million hectares planned with average yields up 10.9 percent.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.  ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,867  100.0(100.0)   185.6    2.8   (n/a)   (14.2)</p>
<p> Maize     3,794   70.9 (63.2)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,004   68.0 (55.0)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770   41.6 (28.1)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	989   29.1 (23.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
